WEBVTT

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:16.690
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:27.700
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:33.230
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.740
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.720
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.520
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.480
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.900
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:11.210
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:23.460
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.960
Hey, let's go
grab lunch.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.000
Okay.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.170
Where should we go?

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.190
Where should we go?
Anything but noodles!

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.540
Ah, this is impossible.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.440
What's impossible?

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.340
Finding a vintage tachometer
for my Toyota hatchback.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:48.010
They're really hard
to get a hold of.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.710
Can't say I share your
passion for car parts.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.580
It goes right up
to 8,000 rpms.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.450
Well, too bad they're
hard to find.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.460
Oh! Aoi!

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:57.960
Hmm?

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.860
Those little omelettes you have
there look delicious!

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:02.690
Would you like one?

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.490
Really?! Thanks! I'll
take you up on that!

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.370
T... Tsujimoto!

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.770
What the heck
is this?

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:18.380
Lunch box specials. Today we
have omelettes and sausages.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.850
Then there's potato cakes
and grilled fish.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.390
Let's not forget the pickles and stewed
vegetables, namely pumpkin and taro!

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.380
And it's awfully darn good,
if I may say so myself.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:31.420
I squeezed the rice balls too much with all
the excitement, so they're a little hard.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.360
But your teeth are all filled, so
I'm sure you'll be just fine.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.660
I didn't know Natsumi was the
type to go all out like this!

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.170
I thought she'd gotten
up really early.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.330
Then I saw the kitchen; it looked
like a bomb had hit it!

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.070
But I think it's
wonderful...

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.810
...having someone eat the lunch
you made especially for them.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.050
I wish I could do that
for someone.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:03.190
What does Aoi go for;
men or women?

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.790
I wouldn't know...

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.860
Hey, don't you make lunches
for that special someone?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.330
A romantic lunch box
for Mr. Nakajima?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.330
Huh? Why would
I? It's not as if...

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.060
Yeah, yeah, here we go again. Quit
being so shy, would you!

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:18.630
I know! When you two go out, you eat
little picnic lunches together!

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.040
I haven't gone on a date with him.
Not since that last time.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.640
What?! Last time? You
mean that time?

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.050
I can't believe
it!

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.750
After all that I did to help things
out between them...

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.420
...and they haven't even gone
on a date since then!

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.990
Nakajima and Miyuki
are both very shy...

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.760
...so it's probably just that the timing
hasn't been right up until now.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.420
Even so, it's taken
much too long!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.200
A kid in elementary school would've
made a move sooner than this!

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.230
What'd you do that
for, Yoriko?!

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.810
Oh, this is
terrible!

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:03.070
FILE. 9
THE LOVE TRIANGLE

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:09.090
So what's this "terrible" thing? Was
there a robbery or something?

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.230
Shh! They'll
hear us!

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.420
I think rather than trying to
deal with this ourselves...

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.890
...it'd be a good idea
to call for backup.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.690
Just be quiet.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:24.160
What?! It's just
Nakajima.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.910
Heey!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.300
What do you think
you're doing?!

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:34.850
Nakajima's been going to that smoke shop
every day now, for three days in a row!

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.750
And what about it?!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.150
He's probably just coming here to
buy some cigarettes, that's all.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.050
But he doesn't
smoke.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.420
Really? Is that
a fact?

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.620
Yes, it is.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.190
Her name is Hiromi Shinohara.
Date of birth; April 6.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.560
Age; 19. Bloodtype; A.
Weight; 46 kg.

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:55.030
Bust; 82 cm. Waist;
58 cm. Hips; 85 cm.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.130
She's the shop owner's eligible daughter,
and the neighbors speak highly of her!

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.370
Jeez, is there anything about
her you don't know?

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.310
Ta-da!

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.950
If only you were so thorough
with your police work!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.600
They're still talking
to each other.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:11.240
They sure seem like
a nice couple.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.060
Oh! I'm
sorry!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:20.790
What are you all looking at? It's not as
if he and I have something going.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.850
What's wrong with Nakajima talking
to someone like that?

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.400
Oh! Miyuki!

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:40.080
Hey, Kobayakawa!
Huh?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.880
Nakajima. Did you
start smoking?

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:50.120
No, I don't
smoke.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.990
Why do you
ask?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.320
I just thought I smelled
it on you.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.660
That's all.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.420
Wha? Smell it...

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.130
Oh! The guy I was with smokes, and the
smell probably got in my clothes!

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:04.470
Really?

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:08.600
Really?
Really! Well. Well, see you!

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.480
What do you think,
Natsumi?

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.280
He sure seems
uncomfortable.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:21.860
He's got to be covering
something up.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.720
He's starting to look like
the unfaithful type!

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:27.120
If that's the case, then
this means war!

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:00.590
<i>"For traffic</i>
<i>safety?"</i>

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.600
<i>"Seeing as we're in</i>
<i>the traffic section."</i>

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.070
<i>"I know it was an order, but</i>
<i>I really had a good time."</i>

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.940
<i>"Me, too."</i>

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.610
Silly!

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.580
Miyuki! Time
to go!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:27.090
Huh?

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:35.720
Well?

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:39.090
Nothing's happened so far. Think
he'll come again today?

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:44.430
Probably. He has to come, otherwise
we're wasting our day off for nothing!

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.570
What's this all about,
anyway?

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:49.180
We're going to ambush
him, of course!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.910
Detective Tokuno said it was the best
way to hamper a culprit's behavior.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:56.080
This isn't an ambush,
this is spying!

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:58.690
I've always wanted
to do this!

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:00.810
But we never have the chance
to in the traffic section!

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:02.960
Just like you.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.990
Here he is!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.060
The culprit has parked in front
of the smoke shop...

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:15.260
...and he's giving the daughter
a warm greeting.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.000
You don't have to tell us about
it, we can see for ourselves!

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:23.670
Considering he's usually shy around girls,
especially hot ones, he seems into it!

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.580
And she doesn't exactly seem
disinterested herself.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.510
He's brought her
a present!

00:08:28.680 --> 00:08:30.550
It's a cake from that really
good bakery near here!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.710
I love their
cake!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.880
It's not fair! He's never bought
us cake from there.

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:39.460
I wonder what they're talking about?
I can't hear a word from here!

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.520
Da-Da-Da!

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:44.120
I figured this was going to happen,
so I brought this stuff along!

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:45.530
You're unreal!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.960
Natsumi, stop
this!

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:51.800
Invading someone's privacy isn't exactly
what I'd call a respectable hobby.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.240
How about knocking it off, seeing
as you have your hands in this?

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.540
Huh? Who,
me?

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:00.270
Shh! I can
hear them!

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.040
Yeah? What are
they saying?

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.810
See? I knew you
were interested!

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.980
No, I...

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.950
Thanks for all your
presents!

00:09:10.060 --> 00:09:12.420
I love the cakes from
this bakery!

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:16.120
Glad to hear that! That
makes me happy.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.890
So, how about
your dad?

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.590
I haven't talked
to him yet.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:26.370
Oh, I see. I was hoping
to be able to meet him.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:27.930
Meet her
father?

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.740
That must
mean...

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:36.280
<i>"Please give me your hand!</i>
<i>No, that's not it."</i>

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:38.410
<i>"I mean, please give me your daughter's</i>
<i>hand in marriage!"</i>

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.490
<i>"I implore</i>
<i>you."</i>

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.130
No way, impossible.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:55.330
Yeah, you're right. Anyway
Nakajima has Miyuki here.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:01.770
M... Miyuki? Oh-oh.

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:06.270
Wait a sec.

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:09.210
Miyuki, wait!

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.130
Hey, what am I supposed
to do?

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.640
Listen, Miyuki.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:42.150
Who says there's anything special going
on between Nakajima and that girl?

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:48.280
And Nakajima's not the type
of guy the girls go for.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:51.980
In fact, there's rarely ever someone
even vaguely interested in him!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.650
<i>Oops.</i>

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:04.430
Miyuki? Miyuki,
speak to me!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:05.840
Natsumi!

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:06.840
Yes?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.100
We're going
shopping!

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:10.040
Huh?

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.160
How are you feeling?
A bit better?

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:06.930
Not especially.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:10.070
Yeah right. That's not what
your face is telling me.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.670
Look at this! Let's
take it for a spin!

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:15.070
No thanks.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.940
Why not? Aha! You're afraid you can't
win against my amazing skills?

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.640
That's not
it at all.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:24.220
I wouldn't be able to
get on wearing this.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.910
Oh yeah. Then I'll
do it on my own.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:29.960
Hey, babe. How about
a race against me?

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.250
This'll be fun!
You're on!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:35.930
How about I give you
a head start?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.070
I'm not gonna need it!

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:41.360
Let's go!

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:49.910
<i>"Nice bike."</i>

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.840
<i>"Oh, Kobayakawa!"</i>

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.840
<i>"You're keeping it in really good shape.</i>
<i>I can tell you care about it."</i>

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.120
<i>"It's my cherished partner. I
trust my life with this bike."</i>

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:08.020
<i>"This is terrible! Nakajima</i>
<i>had an accident!"</i>

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:19.670
<i>"If only I'd been</i>
<i>more careful."</i>

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.500
<i>"Then this wouldn't..."</i>

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.580
<i>"This wouldn't have</i>
<i>happened."</i>

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:35.090
<i>"You served</i>
<i>him well."</i>

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.030
<i>"Your cherished partner</i>
<i>saved your life."</i>

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.320
<i>"Uh-huh..."</i>

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.760
<i>"ln that case... It's your turn to</i>
<i>save your partner this time."</i>

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.570
Miyuki.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:27.740
I lost!

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.170
Miyuki!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.180
<i>Miyuki...</i>

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:39.480
"Bokuto Police Headquarters"

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:43.280
I want a word with
you, Nakajima!

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:44.230
What a pervert!

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.390
You stupid woman! You
stupid, stupid woman!

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:47.490
Now I can't get married!

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.190
Sorry!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.790
If it's Nakajima you're looking
for, today's his day off.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.700
What?!

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:03.700
Just when I really needed to give
him a piece of my mind!

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.610
Ooh, that Nakajima!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:07.310
Just forget it.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.850
What do you mean,
forget it?!

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:12.680
Well, it's not like I ever really
knew how he felt about me.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:17.550
That's what bugs me! Watching you
two dance around drives me crazy!

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:22.220
If you like each other, plant yourself in
front of him and tell him to his face!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.060
Take my example! I'm always
pitching full blast!

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:29.870
The people you plant yourself in front
of come out with black eyes.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:34.700
Miyuki, you know you can't keep
going on like this, don't you?

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.220
Miyuki!

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:50.190
Let's follow
them!

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.260
But...

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.390
You've got to hear it from
the horse's mouth!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:05.870
Hmm?

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:11.610
Oh, no! It's Kobayakawa
and Tsujimoto!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.210
Mr. Nakajima?

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.440
Hang on
tight!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.320
That Nakajima's trying
to get away!

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:23.190
Sonuvabitch! Miyuki!
Step on it!

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:38.900
Just like him. Even with someone on the
back, he's in total control of the bike.

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.800
Hey, this isn't the time to go gaga
over his riding technique!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.040
Turn right!
Here!

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:54.180
Still following me. I knew they
wouldn't be so easy to lose.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:07.790
Nice driving... and
see you later!

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.530
Oh, no!

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:21.580
Hey, Nakajima. Our patrols
aren't always this wild.

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:24.750
Dogs and cats
around here...

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.750
...know where all the
rats hang out, too.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:31.260
Well isn't that admirable?
But it's not as if...

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:34.120
...I run my bike into the ground
like this every day, either!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:42.530
Why that?!

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.370
We're gonna catch that
guy, no matter what!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:55.150
I guess I'm no match for Nakajima's
riding ability.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.870
What's that
grin for?!

00:17:56.980 --> 00:18:00.390
This is your chance to tell him
off in front of that girl!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.760
That's not what you said
before, Natsumi.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:08.720
So?! Just use your policing instincts
to make sure he doesn't get away!

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:09.760
Okie dokie.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:17.130
Nakajima, did you have some business
with those policewomen?

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:22.000
No. Uh, er, it was nothing important.
Thank you very much for asking.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.540
Here comes Kobayakawa.
Just as I thought.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.980
Huh?

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.220
Step on it! We've
almost got him!

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.690
Just leave
it to me!

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:38.620
Miyuki! Natsumi! Come
in! I need help!

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:40.760
Yoriko?!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:55.500
Sorry about this. And thanks
for helping out!

00:18:56.180 --> 00:19:01.010
Unreal. Calling us with that frightened "I
need help!" This isn't what I expected.

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.940
But with all these illegally
parked cars...

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:08.550
...there's no way the two of us could have
possibly finished it all by ourselves!

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:12.390
Don't worry about it. This is but one
aspect of being a police officer.

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:16.530
Snow?

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.760
Yeah, it is!

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.940
I thought it was cold
back there.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:31.540
Have a sip.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.650
Hmm?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.580
"Real Estate" "Ramen"
Hmm?

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:36.720
It'll warm
you up.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.320
Thank you.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.080
Sorry about that
back there.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:46.230
Not at all.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.990
I didn't mean
any harm.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:54.360
I just wanted to keep
it a surprise.

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:59.900
But since you saw me, there's no point
in trying to hide it anymore.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:01.970
Is that?

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:05.710
I knew you
wanted it.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:08.840
The owner of that smoke shop
collects vintage parts.

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:12.110
I heard that he might be able to let
me have one of his tachometers.

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:15.520
But he's always off on trips, so I could
never seem to catch up with him.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.120
The owner of the
smoke shop?

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:22.390
Yeah. So I asked his daughter
to do me a favor.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.560
I found out where her father was
supposed to be today...

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:27.760
...and we went there and got
his permission to take this.

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:31.270
I know it's still a little early, but I
got it as your birthday present.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.430
Is that what
happened?

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:35.940
You don't
like it?

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:40.440
No. I really
love it!

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.450
Thanks a lot,
Nakajima.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:54.650
Car parts for a woman's
birthday. Hmm. I see.

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.260
I don't see anything
wrong with that.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:58.460
Where's the romance
in that?

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:01.870
Oh well. It's just
like them.

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:09.110
Detective Tokuno!

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:13.610
I've made you lunch! Shall
we eat together?

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:17.020
I thought she fancied
the Section Chief.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:20.450
She thinks that he's handsome
and debonair.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:24.010
When she likes a man, she'll be all over
him, but she seems to like lots of men!

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.130
She's got energy
to burn!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.560
Aah! I'm starving!

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.960
Hey! Nakajima!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.230
Hey, Kobayakawa.
What's up?

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:36.370
Here. I made you a lunch box, in
return for my birthday present.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.430
Hope you like
it. Bye!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.580
H... Hey!

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:11.370
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.510
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me lonely.</i>

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:31.560
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:32.090 --> 00:22:39.660
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:48.510
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:57.350
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:57.650 --> 00:23:04.880
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:14.600
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:17.700
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:25.880
"Mysterious Attack"

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:29.580
She's coming!

00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:30.910
You-know-what's coming!

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:31.550
What're you talking about?!

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.020
Like some noodle shop delivery person?

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:35.520
No, no! Nobody that you'd
want showing up!

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:36.660
What? Like a man-
eating shark?

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:38.050
That's not it! A scooter.

00:23:38.230 --> 00:23:41.190
"Scooter?" You mean the
sub-50cc class bikes.

00:23:41.360 --> 00:23:45.320
Trouble comes when least expected.
Scooter comes when least invited.

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:48.970
Next time on You're Under Arrest, File 10,
"The Outlaw Scooter Mama."

00:23:49.100 --> 00:23:51.040
The danger's coming!
